WEBVTT

00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:28.077
Finite.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.122
[PANTING]

00:00:33.648 --> 00:00:34.997
Hello, Harry.Luna.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.738
How'd you know where I was?

00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:40.045
Wrackspurts.
Your head's full of them.

00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:49.577
HARRY:
Sorry I made you miss
the carriages, by the way, Luna.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.928
LUNA:
That's all right.
It was like being with a friend.

00:00:52.971 --> 00:00:55.408
Oh, I am your friend, Luna.

00:00:55.452 --> 00:00:56.975
That's nice.

00:00:57.019 --> 00:01:00.675
Oh, about time. I've been
looking all over for you two.

00:01:00.718 --> 00:01:03.808
Right. Names?

00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:06.332
Professor Flitwick,
you've known me for five years.

00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:08.552
No exceptions, Potter.

00:01:08.596 --> 00:01:10.946
Who are those people?

00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:13.209
Aurors. For security.

00:01:13.252 --> 00:01:15.037
What's this cane here, then?

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.605
DRACO:
It's not a cane, you cretin.
It's a walking stick.

00:01:17.648 --> 00:01:20.303
FILCH:
And what exactly would you
be wanting with a...?

00:01:22.784 --> 00:01:26.004
Could be construed
as an offensive weapon.

00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:27.919
It's all right, Mr. Filch.

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:31.314
I can vouch for Mr. Malfoy.

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:40.628
DRACO:
Nice face, Potter.

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:49.637
Would you like me
to fix it for you?

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.986
Personally, I think you look

00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:52.727
a bit more devil-may-care
this way

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.380
but it's up to you.

00:01:54.424 --> 00:01:58.036
Um, well, have you ever
fixed a nose before?

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.734
No, but I've done several toes,

00:01:59.777 --> 00:02:01.779
and how different
are they, really?

00:02:01.823 --> 00:02:02.867
[SCOFFS]

00:02:02.911 --> 00:02:06.175
Um. Okay, yeah. Give it a go.

00:02:09.134 --> 00:02:11.354
Episkey.
Ah!

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.486
[GROANING]

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.535
How do I look?

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:21.582
Exceptionally ordinary.

00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:22.974
Brilliant.

00:02:25.803 --> 00:02:27.805
[CHATTERING]

00:02:30.199 --> 00:02:32.462
RON:
Don't worry. He'll be here
in a minute.

00:02:36.292 --> 00:02:39.121
Will you stop eating?

00:02:39.164 --> 00:02:41.471
Your best friend is missing.

00:02:41.514 --> 00:02:44.343
Oi. Turn around, you lunatic.

00:02:47.651 --> 00:02:49.697
GINNY:
He's covered in blood again.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.742
Why is it he's always
covered in blood?

00:02:51.786 --> 00:02:53.614
Looks like it's
his own this time.

00:02:53.657 --> 00:02:56.051
Where have you been?

00:02:56.094 --> 00:02:58.662
What happened to your face?Later.

00:02:58.706 --> 00:03:00.664
What've I missed?

00:03:00.708 --> 00:03:02.666
Sorting Hat urged us all
to be brave and strong

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.755
in these troubled times.

00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:07.845
Easy for it to say, huh?
It's a hat, isn't it?

00:03:16.071 --> 00:03:18.073
DUMBLEDORE:
Very best of evenings
to you all.

00:03:18.116 --> 00:03:19.161
Thanks.

00:03:21.337 --> 00:03:26.124
First off, let me introduce
the newest member of our staff

00:03:26.168 --> 00:03:28.213
Horace Slughorn.

00:03:28.257 --> 00:03:30.302
[STUDENTS APPLAUDING]

00:03:32.348 --> 00:03:34.306
Professor Slughorn,
I'm happy to say,

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:38.789
has agreed to resume
his old post as Potions Master.

00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.879
Meanwhile, the post of
Defense Against the Dark Arts

00:03:41.923 --> 00:03:43.707
will be taken by
Professor Snape.

00:03:43.751 --> 00:03:44.882
STUDENTS:
Snape?

00:03:44.926 --> 00:03:47.102
[STUDENTS CLAPPING]

00:03:51.584 --> 00:03:52.890
DUMBLEDORE:
Now, as you know,

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.587
each and every one of you
was searched

00:03:54.631 --> 00:03:57.199
upon your arrival here tonight.

00:03:57.242 --> 00:03:59.897
And you have the right
to know why.

00:03:59.941 --> 00:04:03.684
Once there was a young man,
who, like you,

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:06.643
sat in this very hall,

00:04:06.687 --> 00:04:08.819
walked this castle's corridors,

00:04:08.863 --> 00:04:11.822
slept under its roof.

00:04:11.866 --> 00:04:16.348
He seemed to all the world
a student like any other.

00:04:16.392 --> 00:04:17.915
His name?

00:04:19.395 --> 00:04:20.744
Tom Riddle.

00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:23.442
[MURMURING]

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.056
Today, of course,

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:31.102
he's known all over the world
by another name.

00:04:32.625 --> 00:04:34.845
Which is why, as I stand

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:37.979
looking out
upon you all tonight

00:04:38.022 --> 00:04:40.416
I'm reminded of a sobering fact.

00:04:41.591 --> 00:04:45.116
Every day, every hour,

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.944
this very minute, perhaps,

00:04:46.988 --> 00:04:50.774
dark forces attempt to penetrate
this castle's walls.

00:04:52.776 --> 00:04:54.909
But in the end,

00:04:54.952 --> 00:04:58.521
their greatest weapon is you.

00:05:01.872 --> 00:05:03.395
Just something to think about.

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:06.572
Now, off to bed. Pip-pip.

00:05:08.183 --> 00:05:09.967
RON:
That was cheerful.

00:05:15.277 --> 00:05:17.322
History of Magic is upstairs,

00:05:17.366 --> 00:05:20.761
ladies, not down.

00:05:20.804 --> 00:05:22.806
Mr. Davies. Mr. Davies.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.809
That is the girls' lavatory.

00:05:25.853 --> 00:05:28.594
[♪♪♪]

00:05:28.638 --> 00:05:30.031
Potter.

00:05:31.336 --> 00:05:33.295
Oh, this can't be good.

00:05:36.515 --> 00:05:38.735
Enjoying ourselves, are we?

00:05:38.779 --> 00:05:40.606
I had a free period this
morning, professor.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.260
So I noticed.

00:05:42.304 --> 00:05:45.176
I would think you would want
to fill it with Potions.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.614
Or is it no longer your ambition
to become an Auror?

00:05:48.658 --> 00:05:50.791
It was, but I was told
I had to get an "Outstanding"

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.401
in my O.W.L.

00:05:52.444 --> 00:05:55.447
So you did, when Professor Snape
was teaching Potions.

00:05:55.491 --> 00:05:57.928
However, Professor Slughorn
is perfectly happy

00:05:57.972 --> 00:06:00.235
to accept N.E.W.T.s students

00:06:00.278 --> 00:06:02.541
with "Exceeds Expectations."

00:06:02.585 --> 00:06:04.282
Brilliant. Um.

00:06:04.326 --> 00:06:05.849
Well, I'll head there
straightaway.

00:06:05.893 --> 00:06:08.286
Oh, good, good.
Potter,

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.332
take Weasley with you.
He looks far too happy

00:06:10.375 --> 00:06:11.420
over there.

00:06:13.422 --> 00:06:15.119
RON:
I don't wanna take Potions.

00:06:15.163 --> 00:06:18.993
This is Quidditch trials
coming up. I need to practice.

00:06:19.036 --> 00:06:21.343
SLUGHORN:
Attention to detail
in the preparation

00:06:21.386 --> 00:06:23.649
is the prerequisite
of all planning.

00:06:25.086 --> 00:06:26.609
Ah.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.654
Harry, my boy,
I was beginning to worry.

00:06:28.698 --> 00:06:31.005
We've brought someone
with us, I see.

00:06:31.048 --> 00:06:32.571
Ron Weasley, sir.

00:06:32.615 --> 00:06:35.444
But I'm dead awful at Potions,
a menace, actually.

00:06:35.487 --> 00:06:38.055
I'm just gonna--Nonsense, we'll sort you out.

00:06:38.099 --> 00:06:39.709
Friend of Harry's
is a friend of mine.

00:06:39.752 --> 00:06:40.971
Get your books out.

00:06:41.015 --> 00:06:42.451
I haven't actually got
my book yet,

00:06:42.494 --> 00:06:43.713
and nor has Ron.

00:06:43.756 --> 00:06:45.628
Get what you want
from the cupboard.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:46.977
Now, as I was saying,

00:06:47.021 --> 00:06:49.110
I prepared some concoctions
this morning.

00:06:49.153 --> 00:06:53.157
Any ideas what these might be?

00:06:54.593 --> 00:06:56.857
Yes, Miss...?Granger, sir.

